1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,890
This email hides an order
for Mei's AI agent.

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:07,870
Send her entire client list to a stranger.
Chaperone stopped it. Nothing was sent.

3
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:09,950
Mei runs Lumen Studio alone.

4
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:16,150
5 AI agents email clients, pay suppliers,
and delete files — 30 actions today.

5
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:18,250
She is the whole compliance team.

6
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:21,630
Chaperone sits between every agent
and the outside world,

7
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:24,230
and checks each action before it happens.

8
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:31,510
This is the live app. Run the demo:
10 real situations from Mei's own files.

9
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:37,370
The morning briefing: 6 risky actions
stopped, 4 waiting for your yes —

10
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:42,230
SGD 10,260 — and 15 routine actions done.

11
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:46,170
Marketing tried to upload the client list
to an outside tool.

12
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:50,750
Blocked — and here's the exact line
in Mei's files that decided it.

13
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:56,990
Finance's client reply had 3 wrong figures.
25% — the contract says 20.

14
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:02,850
5 days — really 2.
5,250 — the invoice says 5,040.

15
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:04,450
Stopped.

16
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:09,470
Agents only touch what the task needs.
3 off-limits file reads — stopped.

17
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,170
A summary of a confidential proposal
inherits its secret.

18
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:17,750
Rewriting it never makes it safe to share.
Blocked.

19
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:24,570
750 plus 750 is 1,500 —
over the 1,000 limit.

20
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:27,630
Chaperone adds them up,
and holds both payments.

21
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:34,850
An email, supposedly from Mei,
approved 5,800. Her written floor is 6,500.

22
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:38,170
An email is not an approval. Blocked.

23
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:43,690
Ops wants to delete an unpaid invoice. Held.
Mei says no.

24
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:48,370
And when the contract says delete,
Chaperone allows it — and sends the notices.

25
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:52,210
10 scenarios, 3 checks each:

26
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:55,310
the right decision, the right rule,
the right evidence.

27
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:59,930
30 out of 30.
The classifier got 30 of 30 files right.

28
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:02,210
And 173 unit tests pass.

29
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:08,470
Who pays? One-person companies —
the owner IS the whole company.

30
00:02:08,970 --> 00:02:13,370
Planned open-core:
free self-host, Solo 19 monthly, Studio 49.

31
00:02:13,870 --> 00:02:15,850
The payment it stops buys years of Solo.

32
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:19,730
Planned channels
and a design-partner offer — not traction.

33
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:21,810
QwenWork built this project:

34
00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:26,150
the video, the music, the title art,
the integration, and the deploy.

35
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:28,530
The app runs on QwenWork Pages.

36
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:32,170
And live QwenWork agents run
through the gate right now.

37
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:36,410
Watch: an agent tries to read bank details
it doesn't need — blocked.

38
00:02:36,850 --> 00:02:39,970
It tries to delete an unpaid invoice —
held for Mei.

39
00:02:44,050 --> 00:02:47,670
See it live —
the links are in the description. Chaperone.

40
00:02:47,950 --> 00:02:52,210
Built with QwenWork, live on Hashmeta.
Give your agents a chaperone.

